WEBVTT

00:01:56.199 --> 00:02:00.415
animal models fail to predict
what will happen in humans

00:02:00.415 --> 00:02:03.601
when they're treated with a particular drug.

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.980
So we need better tools.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.733
We need human cells,

00:02:07.733 --> 00:02:10.483
but we need to find a way to keep them happy

00:02:10.483 --> 00:02:12.074
outside the body.

00:02:12.074 --> 00:02:14.980
Our bodies are dynamic environments.

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:16.820
We're in constant motion.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.011
Our cells experience that.

00:02:19.011 --> 00:02:21.820
They're in dynamic environments in our body.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:24.575
They're under constant mechanical forces.

00:02:24.575 --> 00:02:27.031
So if we want to make cells happy

00:02:27.031 --> 00:02:28.460
outside our bodies,

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.986
we need to become cell architects.